# Check compile errors after every change

Do not end a turn after editing app code until you have confirmed it compiles.

1. After writing or patching `.js`, `.jsx`, `.ts`, or `.tsx` files, read the running `next dev` terminal for Turbopack/parse errors (`Parsing ecmascript source code failed`, `Module not found`, compile 500s).
2. Do not use `node --check` on JSX files — it cannot parse JSX and will false-fail.
3. If the terminal shows a parse/compile error, fix it in the same turn before telling the user you are done.
4. Never leave a function body without its `function` / `const` declaration.
